{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013AjrtGK8QgLzez2mM25KFa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t \"number\": 179,\n3\t \"title\": \"Send preedit rectangle (not just cursor rectangle) to support stable IME popup positioning\",\n4\t \"body\": \"### Preflight Checklist\\n\\n- [x] I have read the [Contributing Guidelines](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) for this project.\\n- [x] I agree to follow the [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) that this project adheres to.\\n- [x] I have searched the [issue tracker](https://www.github.com/electron/electron/issues) for a feature request that matches the one I want to file, without success.\\n\\n### Problem Description\\n\\nHi,\\n\\nOn Wayland, CJK input methods currently only get a cursor rectangle from the app. Because the cursor moves while typing Pinyin, the candidate popup jumps around constantly.\\n\\nThe proposed fix in wayland-protocols is to let apps also send a preedit rectangle, so the input method can anchor the popup to the start of the preedit instead of the moving cursor. See the discussion here:\\nhttps://gitlab.freedesktop.org/wayland/wayland-protocols/-/merge_requests/517\\nhttps://gitlab.freedesktop.org/wayland/wayland-protocols/-/merge_requests/521\\n\\nSince Electron apps like VS Code and Slack are very popular on Linux, it would make a huge difference if Electron could send the preedit rectangle via zwp_text_input_v3 (in addition to the cursor rectangle). Without that, input methods can't fix the jumping even if they support the new protocol.\\n\\nIs there any plan to implement this? I'd be glad to test an early build.\\n\\nThanks!\\n\\n### Proposed Solution\\n\\ninput methods\\n\\n### Alternatives Considered\\n\\ninput methods\\n\\n### Additional Information\\n\\n_No response_\",\n5\t \"labels\": [\n6\t  \"enhancement :sparkles:\"\n7\t ],\n8\t \"state\": \"open\",\n9\t \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n10\t \"as_of\": \"2026-08-25T12:19:53Z\",\n11\t \"replay\": true\n12\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"482a9d48-d0ac-41d2-9bc2-e99f6f6503f7","uuid":"99185e80-0233-4f17-b07d-af1ecb21eca4","timestamp":"2026-10-23T12:38:48.201Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/runner/work/cs467-electron-triage/cs467-electron-triage/.triage/issue.json","content":"{\n \"number\": 179,\n \"title\": \"Send preedit rectangle (not just cursor rectangle) to support stable IME popup positioning\",\n \"body\": \"### Preflight Checklist\\n\\n- [x] I have read the [Contributing Guidelines](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) for this project.\\n- [x] I agree to follow the [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) that this project adheres to.\\n- [x] I have searched the [issue tracker](https://www.github.com/electron/electron/issues) for a feature request that matches the one I want to file, without success.\\n\\n### Problem Description\\n\\nHi,\\n\\nOn Wayland, CJK input methods currently only get a cursor rectangle from the app. Because the cursor moves while typing Pinyin, the candidate popup jumps around constantly.\\n\\nThe proposed fix in wayland-protocols is to let apps also send a preedit rectangle, so the input method can anchor the popup to the start of the preedit instead of the moving cursor. See the discussion here:\\nhttps://gitlab.freedesktop.org/wayland/wayland-protocols/-/merge_requests/517\\nhttps://gitlab.freedesktop.org/wayland/wayland-protocols/-/merge_requests/521\\n\\nSince Electron apps like VS Code and Slack are very popular on Linux, it would make a huge difference if Electron could send the preedit rectangle via zwp_text_input_v3 (in addition to the cursor rectangle). Without that, input methods can't fix the jumping even if they support the new protocol.\\n\\nIs there any plan to implement this? I'd be glad to test an early build.\\n\\nThanks!\\n\\n### Proposed Solution\\n\\ninput methods\\n\\n### Alternatives Considered\\n\\ninput methods\\n\\n### Additional Information\\n\\n_No response_\",\n \"labels\": [\n  \"enhancement :sparkles:\"\n ],\n \"state\": \"open\",\n \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n \"as_of\": \"2026-08-25T12:19:53Z\",\n \"replay\": true\n}","numLines":12,"startLine":1,"totalLines":12}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013AjrtGK8QgLzez2mM25KFa","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
